{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "heat_1d_dirichlet_o6",
    "description": "MMS driver: 1-D heat equation u_t = alpha u_xx on the unit interval [0, 1] with inhomogeneous Dirichlet (fixed-value) boundaries, discretized by grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/rules/central_D2_6_dirichlet_bc (sixth-order interior 7-point stencil with sixth-order one-sided boundary-row closures). Manufactured solution u(x,t) = exp(-alpha pi^2 t) sin(pi x) + gL + (gR - gL) x with gL = 0.5, gR = 1.5: the decaying sine satisfies the heat equation and vanishes at both walls, while the steady linear profile gL + (gR - gL) x satisfies u_t = alpha u_xx = 0 and carries the constant wall values u(0) = gL, u(1) = gR. So the exact solution has constant, nonzero wall values, matched by the rule's free names gL, gR (declared as ordinary real parameters; the rule reduces to homogeneous Dirichlet at gL=gR=0). The linear profile is represented exactly by the discrete cell-centered sixth-order operator — its interior stencil and all six boundary closures return identically zero on any linear field (every closure weight-sum is zero) — so the discretization error comes solely from the sine mode. Both the interior 7-point stencil and the boundary closures are O(dx^6), so the error falls at (observed, honestly pinned in tests/conformance/convergence/heat_1d_dirichlet_o6) order ~6; a decaying eigenmode compatible with the walls keeps the closures well-conditioned (the homogeneous discrete Laplacian's spectrum is real and negative, largest real part exactly -pi^2, the fundamental Dirichlet mode). The grid geometry contract (grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/grid.esm) is fulfilled for [0,1]: x0 = 0 and dx = 1/N. gL/gR appear only in the runtime rule body; the build-time ic/reference expressions spell the manufactured solution from literals and the metaparameter N alone (AGENTS.md build-time scope caveat), with the wall value 0.5 and slope 1.0 matching the gL and (gR - gL) parameter values.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:problem",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_1d",
      "equation:heat",
      "mms"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Roache, P. J. (2002). Code verification by the method of manufactured solutions. J. Fluids Eng. 124(1), 4-10.",
        "doi": "10.1115/1.1436090"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Fornberg, B. (1988). Generation of finite difference formulas on arbitrarily spaced grids. Mathematics of Computation 51(184), 699-706.",
        "doi": "10.1090/S0025-5718-1988-0935077-0"
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "Heat": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/rules/central_D2_6_dirichlet_bc.esm"
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "u": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "shape": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "Temperature field over the x index set."
        },
        "alpha": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m^2/s",
          "default": 0.01,
          "description": "Thermal diffusivity."
        },
        "gL": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K",
          "default": 0.5,
          "description": "Prescribed field value at the left wall (the rule's Dirichlet free name), equal to the manufactured wall value u(0) = 0.5."
        },
        "gR": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K",
          "default": 1.5,
          "description": "Prescribed field value at the right wall (the rule's Dirichlet free name), equal to the manufactured wall value u(1) = 1.5."
        },
        "x0": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 0,
          "description": "Left domain edge a = 0 (unit interval): the grid's x0 free name (consumer-supplied geometry contract)."
        },
        "dx": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Grid spacing (b - a)/N = 1/N: the grid's dx free name, resolved inside the rewrite rule's expanded body at evaluation. N is the document-scoped metaparameter, substituted as an integer literal at load (esm-spec 9.7.6), so loader-API rebinding for the convergence sweep keeps dx consistent."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": {
            "op": "ic",
            "args": [
              "u"
            ]
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "i"
            ],
            "args": [],
            "ranges": {
              "i": {
                "from": "x"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "+",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "sin",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        3.141592653589793,
                        {
                          "op": "*",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "-",
                              "args": [
                                "i",
                                0.5
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "op": "/",
                              "args": [
                                1,
                                "N"
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                0.5,
                {
                  "op": "*",
                  "args": [
                    1.0,
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "-",
                          "args": [
                            "i",
                            0.5
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "op": "/",
                          "args": [
                            1,
                            "N"
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": {
            "op": "D",
            "args": [
              "u"
            ],
            "wrt": "t"
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "alpha",
              {
                "op": "D",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "D",
                    "args": [
                      "u"
                    ],
                    "wrt": "x"
                  }
                ],
                "wrt": "x"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "dx",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              1,
              "N"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "mms_dirichlet_o6_decay",
          "description": "Manufactured solution u(x,t) = exp(-alpha pi^2 t) sin(pi x) + gL + (gR - gL) x with alpha = 0.01, gL = 0.5, gR = 1.5. Derivation: the sine mode gives u_t = -alpha pi^2 u_sin and u_xx = -pi^2 u_sin (so u_t = alpha u_xx) with zero wall values; the linear profile is steady (u_t = 0 = alpha u_xx) with wall values gL, gR prescribed to the rule. The linear profile is discretely exact for the sixth-order operator, so the error is the sine mode's, which falls at observed order ~6. References evaluate at cell centers x_i = (i - 1/2)/N, spelled inline per esm-spec 6.6.5 (build-time evaluation folds literals and metaparameters only; the constant 0.5 and slope 1.0 match the gL and (gR - gL) parameter values). The t=0 assertion pins the ic wiring; the t=0.1 assertion bounds the relative L2 error, which at sixth order falls well under 1e-4 for every resolution in the sweep. Exact per-resolution errors are pinned in tests/conformance/convergence/heat_1d_dirichlet_o6/golden/errors.json.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.1
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": {
                "abs": 1e-09
              },
              "reduce": "L2_error",
              "reference": {
                "op": "aggregate",
                "output_idx": [
                  "i"
                ],
                "args": [],
                "ranges": {
                  "i": {
                    "from": "x"
                  }
                },
                "expr": {
                  "op": "+",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "sin",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "*",
                          "args": [
                            3.141592653589793,
                            {
                              "op": "*",
                              "args": [
                                {
                                  "op": "-",
                                  "args": [
                                    "i",
                                    0.5
                                  ]
                                },
                                {
                                  "op": "/",
                                  "args": [
                                    1,
                                    "N"
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    0.5,
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        1.0,
                        {
                          "op": "*",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "-",
                              "args": [
                                "i",
                                0.5
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "op": "/",
                              "args": [
                                1,
                                "N"
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 0.1,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": {
                "abs": 0.0001
              },
              "reduce": "L2_error",
              "reference": {
                "op": "aggregate",
                "output_idx": [
                  "i"
                ],
                "args": [],
                "ranges": {
                  "i": {
                    "from": "x"
                  }
                },
                "expr": {
                  "op": "+",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "exp",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "*",
                              "args": [
                                -0.01,
                                9.869604401089358,
                                0.1
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "op": "sin",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "*",
                              "args": [
                                3.141592653589793,
                                {
                                  "op": "*",
                                  "args": [
                                    {
                                      "op": "-",
                                      "args": [
                                        "i",
                                        0.5
                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                      "op": "/",
                                      "args": [
                                        1,
                                        "N"
                                      ]
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    0.5,
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        1.0,
                        {
                          "op": "*",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "-",
                              "args": [
                                "i",
                                0.5
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "op": "/",
                              "args": [
                                1,
                                "N"
                              ]
                            }
